WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.890
- So the headlines read that
Remington is subpoenaing

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.610
the student records of the first graders

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:04.850
who were shot and killed

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.320
in the Sandy Hook massacre.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.580
So I assume that in this litigation,

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.680
Remington issued a very
broad discovery requests,

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:10.570
something along the lines of

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:13.050
all documents related to the children,

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:14.620
and someone blew it out
of proportion by saying,

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.390
oh, they're specifically
requesting educational records

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:18.640
which have no relevance.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:19.970
Actually not so,

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:21.760
and the headlines are
actually pretty accurate here.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.317
I took a look at the actual
discovery requests which read,

00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:26.297
"Any and all educational
records in your possession

00:00:26.297 --> 00:00:27.627
"including but not limited to,

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.187
"application admission paperwork,

00:00:29.187 --> 00:00:31.607
"attendance records,
transcripts, report cards,

00:00:31.607 --> 00:00:33.287
"disciplinary records, correspondence,

00:00:33.287 --> 00:00:36.047
"and any and all other educational
information and records

00:00:36.047 --> 00:00:39.000
"pertaining to each of the
five first graders at issue."

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.820
So yeah, those are
actually much more specific

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:41.653
than I thought,

00:00:41.653 --> 00:00:43.060
and it's hard to see
what kind of relevance

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:45.830
those documents would have in
this particular litigation.

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:46.980
And so, as a result,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.150
the plaintiff's lawyers are
trying to get a protective order

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.550
to prevent the disclosure of those records

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.820
related to the first grade children

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.620
who were killed in that case.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.810
And they probably stand
a pretty good chance

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.030
of quashing that subpoena,

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.953
but we'll see what happens in court.

